# Security rules

- Never commit `%LocalAppData%/BuildMonitor/settings.json` or log files with user paths.
- Never hardcode PATs, tokens, or connection strings in source or docs.
- Validate project paths from settings — reject traversal outside intended roots when practical.
- `AzureConnectionSecretStore` / `PatSecretStore` use ProtectedData — do not log decrypted values.
- Child processes inherit sanitized env via `DotNetProcessConfigurator` — do not pass host watch pollution through.
- TrayApp runs locally for one user — no multi-tenant auth; still treat monitored project output as untrusted when parsing.

Before ship on sensitive changes, run **`.cursor/skills/security-pass/SKILL.md`** (checklist + report).
